pySMESH: Cartesian_3D with viscous layers says why it cannot offset the shape, and names the
largest total thickness for which the offset works (SMESH V9_16_0; applies after
StdMeshers_Cartesian_VL_offset_makers_leak.patch and StdMeshers_Cartesian_3D_offset_small_cells.patch).

Defect: when the shape cannot be offset by the layer thickness, the compute fails with
"SOLID 1: no message", or with its message cut short, or it succeeds with cells outside the
shape; and the user cannot tell what thickness works.

Symptom: a 2 x 2 x 2 block with a bore of radius 0.4 on its axis, layers on every face (3
layers, factor 1.2), grid spacing 0.25. At 0.29 it meshes. At 0.3 to 0.35: "SOLID 1: no
message". At 0.5, 0.6, 0.65, 0.75, 0.8 and 0.99: "SOLID 1: no message". At 0.7 the compute
either fails with "bad mesh on offset geometry" or succeeds with 13 cells of total volume
0.006, 4 of them inverted, with nodes at x = 2.1, outside the block.

Root cause, measured with an instrumented build: offset by 0.3, the bore reaches radius 0.7
and the walls come to 0.7 from its axis, so the offset surfaces touch. BRepOffset_MakeOffset
then reports IsDone with BRepOffset_NoError and a null shape (at 0.29: a valid solid of
volume 0.739). Thicker, at 0.5 to 0.99, it reports IsDone with a solid that
BRepCheck_Analyzer finds invalid, with 9 faces instead of 7, reaching outside the block
(bounding box -0.1 to 2.1 at 0.7). ViscousBuilder::MakeOffsetSolid (StdMeshers_Cartesian_VL.cxx:913-957)
checks only IsDone and hands either shape on with no error text; its glue of several offset
solids (:963-969) is not checked either. Compute then throws SALOME_Exception with that text
(StdMeshers_Cartesian_3D.cxx:154), or meshes the invalid solid. SMESH_subMesh cuts 7
characters off the text of a SALOME_Exception, for the "Salome " of a prefix
(SMESH_subMesh.cxx:1615-1620), but the std::string constructor of SALOME_Exception adds no
prefix, so even a set message lost its first word.

Change:
* StdMeshers_Cartesian_VL.cxx: MakeOffsetSolid sets an error for an empty offset result
  ("... the layers are too thick for the shape, so that offset surfaces meet ..."), for an
  offset solid that BRepCheck_Analyzer finds invalid ("... so that offset surfaces cross
  ..."), and for a failed glue, and frees the maker it made. Each of these errors ends with
  the largest total thickness for which the offset step works: bisection between 0 and the
  thickness asked for, at most 12 offset steps, each the same offset as MakeOffsetSolid with
  throwaway builders, a step working when every offset solid is non-empty and valid and the
  solids glue together. On the bored block the error names 0.299927 (to 7.3e-05); at 0.285
  the compute meshes, at 0.315 it fails with the same error. SMESH computes a failing SOLID
  twice in one compute; the last bisection is kept (with its shape, thickness and faces with
  layers, under a mutex), so the second call makes no offset step: 12 per compute.
* StdMeshers_Cartesian_3D.cxx: Compute reports the offset error with SMESH_Algo::error
  instead of throwing it.

Not changed: the offset of every shape that can be offset into a valid solid, and the mesh of
every case that meshes; a successful compute makes no extra offset (the bisection runs on the
failure path only); a BRepOffset_MakeOffset that is not done keeps its own error text.

